# Portal env files must never reach a build context.
#
# The bare `.env` / `.env.*` patterns above do NOT cover `portal/.env` — a
# dockerignore pattern without a slash is not applied at every depth, which was
# verified against this exact context rather than assumed. Without the explicit
# paths below, `COPY portal ./` in portal/Dockerfile lands a developer's
# `portal/.env` in the image, and Vite loads it automatically during
# `npm run build` — beneath and regardless of the Dockerfile's ARG/ENV
# allowlist. That is how a shared Platform API bearer token reaches a public
# browser bundle.
#
# No exception for `.env.example` or `.env.e2e`. Neither is an input to the
# production build: the Dockerfile runs `npm run build` (default/production
# mode), which never reads `.env.e2e` — only `vite build --mode e2e` does, and
# that runs from a repo checkout on a dev/CI machine, never inside this image.
# Both files stay committed in the repo; they are simply not shipped into the
# build context.
portal/.env
portal/.env.*
